<title>USA: Great Western may be near $7 bln pact - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Great Western may be near $7 bln pact - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Western Financial Corp is close to a pact to be acquired by Washington Mutual Inc in a stock swap valued at nearly $7 billion, the Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>People familiar with the talks told the paper an announcement could come as early as today.</p>
<p>The report said terms could not be determined, but they are expected to exceed those of H.F. Ahmanson's hostile offer, which is currently valued at $44.10 a share, or more than $6 billion.</p>
